{"name":"Bloom","hex":"#ffaf75","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bloom","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A place in the United States:\nA ghost town in Otero County, Colorado.\nAn unincorporated community and township in Ford County, Kansas.\nA town in Richland County, Wisconsin.\nA number of other townships, including in Illinois, Kansas (2 or 3), Minnesota, Ohio (5), and Pennsylvania, listed under Bloom Township."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bloom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower","wikidata":"Q506"},{"title":"Algal bloom","blocks":[{"text":"An algal bloom or algae bloom is a rapid increase or accumulation in the population of algae in fresh water or marine water systems. It may be a benign or harmful algal bloom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Toxic_Algae_Bloom_in_Lake_Erie.jpg/330px-Toxic_Algae_Bloom_in_Lake_Erie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algal_bloom","wikidata":"Q326139"},{"title":"Bloom (surname)","blocks":[{"text":"Bloom is a surname. Notable people with the surname include:"},{"item